1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,100
Listen to part of a psychology podcast.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:10,060
My brother Alex has always wanted to get a cat. He likes cats better than dogs.

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:16,562
One day he sent me an online article titled "Which Pet is Right for You" and says,

4
00:00:16,562 --> 00:00:19,240
see, even experts agree cats are better.

5
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:23,070
But when I read the article, nowhere did it say that.

6
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:25,411
The article presents balanced facts.

7
00:00:25,411 --> 00:00:31,030
Dogs are loyal and trainable while cats are independent and low maintenance.

8
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,500
My brother was not being dishonest

9
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:37,045
he simply focused only on the parts that praise cats

10
00:00:37,045 --> 00:00:41,180
and skimmed over or dismissed the parts that highlight dogs' advantages.

11
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:44,220
This is called confirmation bias.

12
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,811
Our brains are lazy. They like consistency.

13
00:00:47,811 --> 00:00:56,020
Information that aligns with what we already know is easier to understand and less mentally taxing.

14
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:59,210
So our brains seek it out and filter out the rest.

15
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:05,265
This affects the decisions we make in our daily life as well as in work.

16
00:01:05,265 --> 00:01:08,090
Scientists are not immune to confirmation bias.

17
00:01:08,090 --> 00:01:15,077
Researchers may unintentionally design experiments or interpret data in ways that support their hypotheses,

18
00:01:15,077 --> 00:01:19,070
overlooking results that do not fit their expectations.

19
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:24,140
Flawed conclusions in scientific studies can lead to serious consequences.

20
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:28,200
So what can we do to minimize confirmation bias?

21
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:33,360
The first step is to recognize the existence of confirmation bias

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,180
Know that you might be biased.

23
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:40,010
Then actively seek out information that challenges your beliefs.

24
00:01:40,010 --> 00:01:43,780
Don't only talk with people who hold the same views as yours

25
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:47,250
and slow down. Don't make hasty decisions.
